{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>If you lie among the sheepfolds</b> — like the rims of a pot, which are like blackness. And the meaning: do not fear the enemy, for even if you dwell among the rims, you are white like a dove, which is plated in silver." "<b>her pinions</b> — like \"Oh that I had wings like a dove\" (Psalm 55:7)." "<b>in greenish gold</b> — the appearance of gold, like \"and all faces are turned to greenness\" (Jeremiah 30:6). And the meaning: soon you will shake off the blackness and the white will be seen."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:08.319866902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}